course: dictionary
lesson: 10333
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Trainer is a good example. «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone: the tick on your trainers, the font in your book» is about shoes, because you can tick your trainers and your book has a font.
explain: Look for clue words. In «Trainers use a whistle to say "yes, that's right" at the exact moment, then give a fish», the clues are whistle and fish. Those clues show that trainers here are people who teach animals to do things. Try the meaning in the sentence: does "people who teach" fit? Yes, so that is the meaning.
explain: Ask yourself: what does the sentence seem to be about? If it is about sport, a team, or practice, the meaning will often be different than if it is about clothes or shoes. Once you have a meaning, read the whole sentence again to check it makes sense.
fact: Trainer has three main meanings: a person who teaches a sport or skill, soft sports shoes, and a thing used for practice.
fact: «Trainers» as shoes is British, Irish and Australian English. Americans say sneakers.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, people also say runners or sneakers for these shoes.
fact: A personal trainer, a dog trainer and a horse trainer are all people who teach or coach.
fact: Training wheels, also called stabilisers in Britain, are a thing used for practice when learning to ride a bike.
exercise: «At his cousin's birthday they stand round the trampoline staring at their trainers.» What are the trainers here? | *Soft sports shoes | Long, thin tubes of rubber | A kind of trampoline | People who teach sports
exercise: «Trainers use a whistle to say "yes, that's right" at the exact moment, then give a fish.» What does trainers mean here? | Teams that play football | *People who teach animals to do something | Shoes for running | Things used for practice, like a cup
exercise: Which one is a thing used for practice, not a person? | A personal trainer | A football trainer | A dog trainer | *Training wheels on a bike
test: «On PE day you wear or pack the sports clothes and trainers the school asks for.» What does trainers mean here? | A person who teaches | A thing used for practice | *Soft sports shoes | A coach of horses
test: A child in Sydney says, "I need new runners for PE." Which British word means the same kind of shoe? | Dog trainer | Personal trainer | Trainer cup | *Trainers
exam: Which sentence uses trainer to mean a person? | "The trampoline was in the garden" | "I need to do up my trainers before PE" | *"The dog trainer taught Biscuit to sit and walk on a lead" | "The training wheels helped Sam learn to ride"
